# GitHub App (github.com > Settings > Developer settings > GitHub Apps > New GitHub App)
#   Repository permissions: Metadata (read), Contents (read), Pull requests (read)
#   Subscribe to events: Push, Pull request (installation events are always delivered)
#   Callback URL: http://localhost:8000/integrations/github/setup
#     and enable "Request user authorization (OAuth) during installation"
#     (GitHub disables Setup URL in this mode; leave it empty)
#   Webhook URL: {public base}/integrations/github/webhooks (use smee.io or ngrok locally)
#   Webhook secret: same value as GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET
# GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY is the downloaded .pem contents on one line, with newlines written as \n
GITHUB_APP_ID=
GITHUB_APP_SLUG=
GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY=
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
GITHUB_FRONTEND_REDIRECT=http://localhost:5173/settings/github?status=
